OVERVIEW
========
This is a sample TIP client, written in C. The client is a command-line program
that supports the following functionality:

	- connect to a TIP access point
	- send streaming request
	- write feed to a logfile
	- client failover through XMAPI (provided that a secondary TIP access
	  point is specified on the command line)
	- soft restart and recovery from logfile

BUILDING THE SAMPLE CLIENT
==========================
The source tarball contains the sample client and XMAPI. The supplied makefile
builds both components.

The makefile is created for Sun Solaris 10 and SunStudio 11.

To unpack the source tarball and build the client:

	$ gunzip -c tipclient.tar.gz | tar xf -
	$ cd tipclient
	$ make

The makefile will build both XMAPI and tipclient.

RUNNING THE SAMPLE CLIENT 
=========================
The client accepts the following command line:

tipclient -a address -u uid -p pwd {-R|-B} [-s scope] [-v] [-d YYYYMMDD] [-x protversion] [-b n] [-e n] [-z][-q queuealert]

        -a address       DDS address hostname:port. Specify multiple addresses to enable fail-over on error.
        -u uid           Account name to use when connecting.
        -p pwd           Password to use when connecting.
        -R               Request realtime (RTr) data
        -B               Request basic (BDa) data}
        -s scope         Basic data scope (numeric value).
        -v               Increase verbosity level; each occurence of this argument
                         increases the amount of messages displayed.
        -d YYYYMMDD      Use this date when requesting data.
        -x protversion   Specify protocol version. Default is no protocol version.
        -b n             Recover from this sequence number.
        -e n             Recover to this sequence number.
        -z               Enable compression.
        -q queuealert    Queue alert treshold, ms.

Example
-------

To retrieve realtime data (with all basic data) for the current day:

    ./tipclient -a hostname:port -u test -p secret -R

DESIGN OVERVIEW
===============
The client is a single-threaded program that uses XMAPI to handle connections to TIP access points.

The overall runtime structure looks something like this:

	parse command line
	initialize
	soft restart from existing logfile
	message pump
		while not connected
			connect and send streaming request from next sequence number
			sleep
		end while

		get next message
		write message to logfile
		process message
	end message pump
	disconnect

The source code is divided into three files:

	main.c		The main program, message pump, soft restart etc.
	utils.c 	Common utility functions
	tiputils.c 	TIP utility functions

For details, please see the source code.

